;
; expect: `@key` on a `#query` rejects directly. `@key` declares a
; relation-local access path and rides ONLY on `#local`/`#export`; a query's
; calling convention is its bound/free parameters, so a key on a query has no
; semantic referent. The query parser draws a targeted witness in state 6
; rather than the generic "unexpected tokens following declaration" cascade.
#message edge_2(u64 A, u64 B).
#query path(bound u64 A, free u64 B) @key(A).
path(A, B) : edge_2(A, B).
